# Kernel defect MERGE-REFERENCE-TO-OPERAND (measured 2026-10-11 on 2a711a13 with this form; R6-2 (4)): a named Structure's
# reference to another operand of the same merge -- Holder's `p: Model`, `R: merge: Model Holder` -- is copied as a link to
# the operand's discarded intermediate copy (lmx_copy_absorb rewrites a copied Structure's slots and parent, not a reference
# cell's pointee): the read aborted natively ("a field of an admitted reference is not carried by its value (no record, or a
# hole)") and was INVALID walked.  Refused where the merge stands until the kernel slice; the required positive is OPEN.
Model:
    int: v 11
end: Model
Holder:
    p: Model
    int: k 3
end: Holder
R: merge: Model Holder
int: code 7
if: R\p\v != 11
    code: 81
if: R\k != 3
    code: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
